---
export interface Props {
  contactHref?: string;
}
const { contactHref = '/contact' } = Astro.props;
---
<h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="policy-updated">Last updated 13 September 2026</p>

<div class="policy">
  <p>
    Chess Tournament Calendar is run on a non-profit basis. It doesn't sell anything, doesn't run ads, and has no
    accounts to sign up for. This page sets out the data that does get collected, who receives it, and how to stop
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible for this site</h2>
  <p>
    Chess Tournament Calendar is run on a non-profit basis from Finland, and is the data controller for the
    purposes of the GDPR. For any question about this policy, or to exercise any of the rights listed below, use
    the <a href={contactHref}>contact form</a>; it reaches the person who runs the site directly.
  </p>

  <h2>What gets collected</h2>

  <h3>Analytics</h3>
  <p>
    This site uses Google Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages get used. It sets cookies in your
    browser and collects your IP address, approximate location, device and browser type, the pages you view, and
    the site you arrived from. This is used only to understand what's worth improving. It is never used to
    identify you personally, and it is never sold or shared with anyone beyond Google.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google acts as a processor for this data and may transfer it to the United States under the EU–US Data
    Privacy Framework. Google's own handling is governed by
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>, and
    how long the data is kept is set by the retention setting on the Analytics property. Chess Tournament Calendar
    does not keep a separate copy.
  </p>
  <p class="note">
    If you'd rather not be counted, there's a switch under <a href="#opt-out">How to opt out</a> below that turns
    analytics off for good. It stops the script from loading at all, rather than loading it and discarding what it
    sends.
  </p>

  <h3>Tournament data</h3>
  <p>
    The tournament listings themselves come from <a href="https://chess-results.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">chess-results.com</a>
    and <a href="https://ratings.fide.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ratings.fide.com</a>. This is public
    tournament information — dates, locations, entry lists, standings — not data about you as a visitor.
  </p>

  <h3>Hosting</h3>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub receives and logs the usual server request data, including IP
    addresses, as part of serving the pages. See
    <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>The contact form</h3>
  <p>
    If — and only if — you submit the <a href={contactHref}>contact form</a>, the name (optional), email address,
    topic and message you type are sent through
    <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web3Forms</a>, which forwards them to a
    private email inbox. That's used to reply to you and nothing else. Messages stay in that inbox until they're
    deleted; ask via the form and yours will be removed.
  </p>

  <h3>Your language and favorites</h3>
  <p>
    Your chosen language, and any tournaments you mark as a favorite, are saved in your browser's local storage
    so the site remembers them next time. This never leaves your device, isn't a cookie, and isn't seen by anyone.
    It goes away if you clear your browser data.
  </p>

  <h2>What is not collected</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No accounts, logins or passwords — there's nothing to register for.</li>
    <li>No advertising or advertising trackers.</li>
    <li>No social media pixels or embedded trackers.</li>
    <li>No payment data of any kind.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    Hosting logs and the contact form rest on legitimate interest: serving the site securely and answering people
    who write in. Your language and favorites are strictly necessary for a setting you asked for. Analytics can be
    turned off at any time using the switch below, and stays off on this browser once you do.
  </p>

  <h2 id="opt-out">How to opt out</h2>
  <p>
    The switch below is the direct route: turn it off and this site stops loading Google Analytics for you
    entirely, so nothing is requested from Google and no data about your visit leaves this page.
  </p>

  <div class="optout" id="optout" hidden>
    <div class="optout-row">
      <span class="optout-label">Analytics in this browser</span>
      <button type="button" class="optout-btn" id="optoutBtn">Turn off</button>
    </div>
    <p class="optout-status" id="optoutStatus" role="status">Analytics is currently on.</p>
    <p class="optout-caveat">
      This preference is stored in this browser only, so you'd need to set it again on another device — and,
      awkwardly, clearing your browsing data also clears it.
    </p>
  </div>
  <noscript>
    <p class="note">You have JavaScript disabled, so Google Analytics isn't loading at all and there's nothing to opt out of.</p>
  </noscript>

  <p>These all work too, and don't depend on this site honouring anything:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Block or clear cookies for this site in your browser settings. Nothing here breaks if you do.</li>
    <li>Use a browser that blocks trackers by default — Brave, DuckDuckGo, or Firefox with Enhanced Tracking Protection set to Strict. These stop Analytics outright.</li>
    <li>On a desktop browser, install <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Analytics opt-out add-on</a>, which applies to every site using Analytics. There's no mobile version.</li>
    <li>Private browsing helps, but less than it looks: it clears the cookies afterwards rather than preventing the data being collected in the first place.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you can ask for a copy of your data, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, object to it being
    processed, or ask for processing to be restricted. Use the <a href={contactHref}>contact form</a> and it will be
    handled without charge, normally within a month.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you aren't satisfied with the response, you can complain to the Finnish Data Protection Ombudsman
    (<a href="https://tietosuoja.fi/en/home" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tietosuoja.fi</a>), or to the data
    protection authority in your own EU country.
  </p>
</div>

<script>
  // The opt-out control. The flag it writes is read by Base.astro before the
  // Analytics script is injected, so opting out means the script is never
  // requested at all — Google receives nothing, not even the IP address a
  // blocked-but-loaded script would still have leaked.
  (function () {
    var KEY = 'ctc-analytics-optout';
    var box = document.getElementById('optout');
    var btn = document.getElementById('optoutBtn');
    var status = document.getElementById('optoutStatus');
    if (!box || !btn || !status) return;

    function readOptedOut() {
      try {
        return localStorage.getItem(KEY) === '1';
      } catch (e) {
        return null;
      }
    }

    function render(optedOut) {
      if (optedOut === null) {
        btn.hidden = true;
        status.textContent = "This browser is blocking site storage, so the preference can't be saved here. One of the options below will work instead.";
        return;
      }
      btn.textContent = optedOut ? 'Turn back on' : 'Turn off';
      status.textContent = optedOut
        ? 'Analytics is off. Nothing is being loaded from Google on any page you visit here.'
        : 'Analytics is currently on.';
    }

    btn.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var next = !readOptedOut();
      try {
        if (next) localStorage.setItem(KEY, '1');
        else localStorage.removeItem(KEY);
      } catch (e) {
        render(null);
        return;
      }
      window['ga-disable-G-PME2NXTXQR'] = next;
      render(next);
    });

    render(readOptedOut());
    box.hidden = false;
  })();
</script>
